1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,420
Come in, Amy, Ravi.
Let's talk about your placements.

2
00:00:03,985 --> 00:00:06,700
Amy, you were hoping to get
into publishing, weren't you?

3
00:00:06,875 --> 00:00:09,760
I was, but none of the
publishers had space.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,640
So I ended up at the local paper,
the Evening Post, in their newsroom.

5
00:00:13,930 --> 00:00:16,640
And Ravi, did the engineering
company work out?

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:18,520
No, that fell through.

7
00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:21,980
I was with the city council in the
end, in the planning department.

8
00:00:22,590 --> 00:00:24,860
They worked with architects
a lot, which was interesting.

9
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:27,940
How long were you each there?
Four weeks is the minimum.

10
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:33,220
We both did six. I could have stayed
for eight, but my course started again.

11
00:00:33,525 --> 00:00:35,740
Amy, what did you struggle with at first?

12
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:40,100
I expected the deadlines to be the problem,
and the software took a day or two.

13
00:00:40,610 --> 00:00:44,120
But what really scared me was phoning
members of the public for comments.

14
00:00:44,414 --> 00:00:45,900
I'd have hated that.

15
00:00:46,195 --> 00:00:47,920
Ravi, what did your days involve?

16
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:52,600
I sat in on a couple of public meetings,
and there was a traffic study going on.

17
00:00:52,985 --> 00:00:56,900
But most of the time, I was going through
people's applications for building work,

18
00:00:57,049 --> 00:00:58,449
to see if they met the regulations.

19
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:00,220
And how was your supervisor?

20
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:01,680
Very busy.

21
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:06,200
Sometimes I'd wait a day for a reply,
and some weeks I had loads to do.

22
00:01:06,669 --> 00:01:10,000
But whenever she commented on
my work, it was really worth having.

23
00:01:10,319 --> 00:01:12,420
Amy, what do you think you got better at?

24
00:01:12,679 --> 00:01:15,940
People assume it'd be
interviewing, and I did plenty of that.

25
00:01:16,304 --> 00:01:19,480
But the real change was learning
to say things in fewer words.

26
00:01:19,854 --> 00:01:22,340
My editor cut everything I wrote by half.

27
00:01:22,580 --> 00:01:23,485
Excellent.

28
00:01:23,509 --> 00:01:24,900
Now, about the reports.

29
00:01:25,389 --> 00:01:27,597
Don't spend pages on
how the organisation is

30
00:01:27,621 --> 00:01:29,892
structured, or describing
your daily routine.

31
00:01:30,519 --> 00:01:33,780
I want to read about what you
personally gained from the experience.

32
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:34,890
Fine.

33
00:01:34,914 --> 00:01:36,860
Ravi, did it help with your career plans?

34
00:01:37,239 --> 00:01:40,840
I'd hoped to make some contacts
for a job, and I didn't really.

35
00:01:41,359 --> 00:01:44,580
And I still don't know which area
of planning I want to specialise in.

36
00:01:45,099 --> 00:01:48,040
But I did find out that
I'm happier in a big public

37
00:01:48,064 --> 00:01:51,132
organisation than I would
be in a small private firm.

38
00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:52,380
Were there any problems?

39
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:53,600
Money, mainly.

40
00:01:53,960 --> 00:01:54,960
The bus fares.

41
00:01:55,074 --> 00:01:56,740
It was two buses each way.

42
00:01:57,020 --> 00:01:58,020
Same for me.

43
00:01:58,239 --> 00:02:02,660
The hours were fine, and the training
was good, but getting there cost a fortune.

44
00:02:03,189 --> 00:02:05,420
There is a travel grant for exactly that.

45
00:02:05,959 --> 00:02:10,180
It's not new, it's been running for years,
and it covers buses as well as trains.

46
00:02:10,740 --> 00:02:14,180
But the money is limited, and by
the time you two asked, it had all gone.

47
00:02:14,770 --> 00:02:16,620
You really needed to apply much sooner.

48
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:18,420
Nobody told us.

49
00:02:18,740 --> 00:02:21,320
Now, the deadline for
the report isn't this Friday.

50
00:02:21,740 --> 00:02:23,540
You've got until the Friday of next week.

51
00:02:23,820 --> 00:02:25,280
And how long should it be?

52
00:02:26,220 --> 00:02:30,400
Last year's limit was 2,000
words, but it's been raised to 3,000.

53
00:02:30,734 --> 00:02:32,840
Should we put our
timesheets in the appendix?

54
00:02:33,580 --> 00:02:36,360
There's no need for timesheets,
or a letter from your employer.

55
00:02:36,844 --> 00:02:39,220
Include examples of things
you actually produced.

56
00:02:39,595 --> 00:02:40,720
Who marks the reports?

57
00:02:41,084 --> 00:02:44,920
Employers aren't involved, and we don't
use an external examiner for placements.

58
00:02:45,435 --> 00:02:47,260
Two tutors read each one separately.

59
00:02:48,010 --> 00:02:49,880
There's also the placement
session next term.

60
00:02:50,404 --> 00:02:53,780
Last year, students gave talks,
but people found them rather dull.

61
00:02:54,180 --> 00:02:56,460
So this year, I'd like you
each to make a poster.

62
00:02:56,940 --> 00:02:57,940
When is it?

63
00:02:58,110 --> 00:02:59,110
Not week one.

64
00:02:59,265 --> 00:03:00,520
There's too much going on then.

65
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:01,840
It'll be week three.

66
00:03:02,165 --> 00:03:03,220
Will employers be there?

67
00:03:03,580 --> 00:03:06,006
A few might come, but
it's really aimed at students

68
00:03:06,007 --> 00:03:08,360
in their first year, before
they apply for placements.

69
00:03:08,950 --> 00:03:10,540
So, what advice would you give them?

70
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:14,620
People say apply early, but honestly,
the deadlines were quite generous.

71
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:17,200
I'd tell them to keep a journal every day.

72
00:03:17,445 --> 00:03:18,620
I forgot so much.

73
00:03:18,980 --> 00:03:19,876
I agree.

74
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:24,100
And I'd say ask for feedback regularly,
rather than waiting until the end.

75
00:03:24,265 --> 00:03:25,360
Yes, definitely.

76
00:03:25,839 --> 00:03:29,040
Visiting the workplace first
is nice, but it isn't essential.

77
00:03:29,515 --> 00:03:31,814
And the distance
didn't really matter, so I

78
00:03:31,838 --> 00:03:34,472
wouldn't tell them to
choose somewhere near home.

79
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:35,326
Good.

80
00:03:35,350 --> 00:03:36,380
I'll pass those two on.

